 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 242732,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/7a0ad604c4f1f7a0.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n(credit: modification of work by Mduma, S.A.R., et al./<i>Journal of Animal Ecology</i>)\n</figure>\n",
   "stem_html": "<p>Wildebeests migrate over 1800 miles each year in search of ripe grass. A research study compared the amount of rainfall and the survival rate of adult wildebeests. The graph shows their findings. The bars show the rainfall amount and the line shows the survival rate.</p>\n<p>Make a claim based on this information.</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 760390,
     "content_html": "The survival curve follows the rainfall with about one month time lag. Rainfall is a major factor that affects survival of wildebeest."
    },
    {
     "id": 760389,
     "content_html": "The survival curve is not affected by rainfall. Rainfall is not a factor in wildebeest survival."
    },
    {
     "id": 760388,
     "content_html": "The survival curve exactly matches the rainfall curve. This indicates availability of drinking water is a major factor in wildebeest survival."
    },
    {
     "id": 760387,
     "content_html": "Wildebeest survival is negatively affected by large amounts of rainfall. This indicates rainfall brings dangers which the wildebeests cannot avoid."
    }
   ],
